      "title": "Gavin Newsom signs laws to protect California workers from AI threat",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/30/gavin-newsom-california-ai-threat",
      "description": "<p>Democratic governor sharply critical of Donald Trump for not passing comprehensive federal AI regulations</p><p>Governor Gavin Newsom signed laws Wednesday aimed at protecting California workers from the threats of artificial intelligence , including potential job losses and workplace surveillance.</p><p>The laws ban employers from using the technology to predict a worker’s emotional state by using their biometric data, require employers to send written notices to workers if AI is responsible for mass layoffs and ban employers from relying on AI to decide to fire someone.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/30/gavin-newsom-california-ai-threat\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-01T00:17:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "California governor Newsom signs laws to protect workers from AI risks",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/california-governor-signs-laws-to-protect-workers-from-ai-risks-126100100063_1.html",
      "description": "California Gov. Gavin Newsom signed laws Wednesday aimed at protecting workers from the threats of artificial intelligence, including potential job losses and workplace surveillance.\nHe also signed an executive order to require state agencies to continue to refer to the technology as \"artificial intelligence\" instead of the term \" super intelligence \" President Donald Trump recently ordered US diplomats to use.\n\"AI should expand opportunity - not come at the expense of workers and families,\" the Democratic governor said in a statement. \"As this technology reshapes the workplace, California is putting people at the centre.\"\nNewsom sharply criticised Trump at an hourlong event with reporters Wednesday for not passing comprehensive federal AI regulations at a time when industry leaders are warning about the technology's risks. Trump said Tuesday that top tech leaders signed a voluntary accord to \"self-police\" AI development.\nThe governor signed a law this month requiring operators of",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-01T02:30:26"
    },
